{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli at the age of 12 after his father was assassinated by the Hashshashin in 1152.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father was the Count of Tripoli and his mother was the sister of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. After his father's assassination in 1152 Raymond III succeeded him as Count of Tripoli at the age of 12. Due to his young age the regency was held by his mother Hodierna.\n\nRaymond III was a vassal of the King of Jerusalem and was required to provide military support to the kingdom. In 1153 Raymond III was present at the siege of Ascalon which was led by King Baldwin III. The siege was successful and the city was captured from the Fatimids.\n\n*The Regency of Amalric I*\nIn 1157 King Baldwin III died and his brother Amalric I succeeded him as King of Jerusalem. Amalric I took over the regency of Tripoli from Hodierna and Raymond III was placed under his guardianship. Amalric I played a significant role in the early life of Raymond III and helped him to consolidate his power in Tripoli.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin*\nIn 1187 Raymond III was present at the Battle of Hattin which was fought between the Crusader army and the Ayyubid army led by Saladin. The Crusader army was defeated and many of its leaders including King Guy of Lusignan were captured. Raymond III was also captured but was later released. He died in 1187 while on his way to Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35264554619789124}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0